Vision self-review (both PNGs):
  - No setup modal (demo mode pre-seeded); top bar: "corral fleet" +
    read-only + demo data chips; banner states the read-plane boundary.
  - Board: "fleet board", 9 agents, live dot; sections blocked (1) ->
    demo-alpha (3) -> demo-bravo (2) -> demo-charlie (2) -> demo-delta (1)
    -> no repo (1); blocked agent cross-listed in its repo group (v2 pinned
    design, same as the iOS board).
  - Rows: name / time-in-state / raw token chip (! blocked / O working /
    □ idle / ? unknown) / repo · branch / pane ref. No clipped or
    half-truncated pane refs (pane_reference keeps the full final two
    segments, mirroring iOS; regression covered in model tests).
  - No overflow, no blank middle rows; desktop capture shows the same board
    full-width at 1280x800.

Drill-in (recents v1) and the first-open setup panel are exercised by the
crate's unit tests (board_frame hydration/refresh wiring + register/settings
surface probes) and were not re-shot here (headless shell cannot click).

